{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun feeling…artificial. The light seemed too bright, the colors too saturated. He sat up in bed, the floral pattern of the comforter unnervingly crisp. His bedroom was familiar, yet…off. The posters on the wall were all characters from \"Aethelgard Online,\" the fantasy MMORPG he'd played religiously for the last five years. A notification pinged from a device on his nightstand – a health bar, a mana pool, and a quest log scrolling across the screen. Panic tightened his chest. He reached out, his hand passing *through* the nightstand. He tried to scream, but the sound that came out was a synthesized chime. He was *in* the game. He was Kaelen, the elven ranger he’d painstakingly crafted, complete with a ridiculously long, flowing silver braid.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of his room, the hallway stretching impossibly long and rendered with a level of detail he'd never witnessed in the game. NPCs walked past, their movements jerky and predictable, repeating phrases from their programmed scripts. A notification popped up: \"Tutorial Quest: Gather 5 Moonpetal Flowers for Elara the Herbalist.\" Arthur, or rather, Kaelen, stared at the screen, a wave of despair washing over him. This wasn’t a dream; this was real. He was trapped in a world of quests, monsters, and pre-determined storylines. He had no idea how to get out, or even if he *could*. All he knew was that he had to gather some blasted flowers.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.4037037789821625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00023040501400828362}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08387291431427002}, {"token": "▁morning", "logprob": -1.023587703704834}, {"token": "▁sun", "logprob": -0.10218741744756699}, {"token": "▁feeling", "logprob": -1.2940853834152222}, {"token": "…", "logprob": -0.7490172982215881